X.TH WAND 6 "4 March 1988" "Newwords+ Manual"
X.\"@(#)wand.6 1.1 88/03/04 SMI;
X.SH NAME
Xwand \- Runs the game "Wanderer".
X.SH SYNOPSIS
Xwand [ -s | -e file | -m | -c | [ -f ] [ -r file ] | -v | -t file ]
X.SH DESCRIPTION
XWanderer is a game similar to Boulderdash, Repton, XOR and others. A full
Xdescription of how to play the game is given upon execution. The hiscore table
Xholds only 15 scores, and the name displayed is taken from the environment
Xvariable NAME. If you wish to have a different alias without changing this
Xvariable, you can set the variable NEWNAME before playing by putting the
Xcommand
X.PP
Xsetenv NEWNAME "My name"
X.PP
Xand then typing update. Also, the keys may be redefined by setting the
Xvariable NEWKEYS in the same way - eg
X.PP
Xsetenv NEWKEYS 'aznm'
X.PP
Xin your .cshrc to get the keys a,z,n,m. Note that the order is important.
XAs well as these keys, '!' will show the whole map, '~' will jump levels,
Xand '?' will provide help.
X.PP
XBy using the -r option you can record the moves you make in a game. Use
Xthis facility to make solution files to mail to me with any screens you send.
X.PP
XThe hiscore table editor is RESTRICTED under a password to prevent you all
Xdeleting each others hiscores. If you can get into it, type the number of the
Xentry to delete it, and 0 to exit.
X.PP
XYou can save games with the 'S' key, and restore with 'R'. If you want to put
Xthe files in a specific place, you can set the environment variable SAVENAME
Xto the file - eg
X.PP
Xsetenv SAVENAME ~/.wanderersave
X.PP
XThe help screen can be accessed by pressing '?'.
X.SH THE GAME
XThe game consists of a number of screens which must be solved in succession
Xunless the password for a later screen is known. Passwords for the screens are
Xgiven on completion. To complete
Xa screen, you must collect all the 'treasure',
Xincluding all 'baby monsters', and then walk into the 'exit'. A
Xfull description of the objects in the game is available on the help
Xscreen, by pressing '?' during the game.
X.PP
XAlso in the game are arrows, boulders and balloons, which move in different
Xdirections, off of one another and slopes, and sometimes through each
Xother. These can sometimes be pushed, but more often than not they block your
Xway to the treasures.
XBy careful manipulation you should be able to make it to
Xthe exit after collecting all of the treasure.
X.PP
XThe 'thingys' can be pushed in any direction by either you or by the boulders,
Xarrows, and balloons. They will remain stationary if not pushed.
X.PP
XPoints are awarded for collecting treasure or earth or
Xfor caging baby monsters or killing big monsters. Also for using the teleport
Xand a bonus for completing the screen. If you use the password to jump levels,
Xyou do not recieve the bonus.
X.PP
XBy pressing 'W' you can redraw the screen, and '#' will switch between the
Xicon style and single character. '!' wil display the map in icon mode, and '?'
Xwill display the help screen. Finally, '~' will prompt for a password to jump
Xlevels. The masterpassword will give a prompt for the required level
Xnumber, and then respond with the correct password before jumping. If the file
X'no_pws' is readable in the screens directory, then pressing '~' will just
Xcause a request for the required screen number. On no account may anyone
Xwho has not given the masterpassword jump back a level.
X.SH THE EDITOR
XThe argument give is the file used for editing. If this cannot be read,
Xit is created. If it
Xcannot be created, a file in /tmp is used. Also, if the file can be read
Xbut not written, a file in /tmp of the form '/tmp/screen.XXXX' is used
Xwhere 'XXXX' is the current process id.
X.PP
X The wanderer keys move the cursor about the edit window,
Xwhere you can add any symbols requirse to the map. Pressing '"' will take the
Xnext keypress literally, so this method may be used to add certain lower case
Xletters. A list of active characters is displayed down the righthand side
Xof the screen with their meanings.
X.PP
XTo play the game, press either 'p' to play with the iconic screen, or 'n'
Xto play with the full screen. When you are in the game, you will recieve an
Xextra 'memory' option on the righthand side of the screen. This allows you to
X'record' moves in a solution to be replayed after changes to the screen.
X.PP
XPressing '(' will start recording from the beginning of the memory, and ')'
Xwill stop recording. At any point during recording, '-' will add a
X'checkpoint'. This will cause the program to return control to the user during
Xplayback when it reaches this point, without moving the memory pointer.
XPressing '+' will then continue playing, or '&' will start recording from this
Xpoint, leaving the previous data unaffected.
X.PP
XThe play key is '*'. This will cause the recorded moves to be played back
Xuntil either (1) you reach a checkpoint ( press '+' to continue ), (2) you
Xreach the end of the recording, or (3) you die.
XTo extend the recording in memory, play through to the end
Xand then press '&'.
X.PP
XWhen in the editor, C-W will save the moves memory and C-R will load a file
Xinto the memory. The number of moves available can be changed with 'm', and
Xthe name of the screen with 'c'.
X.PP
XPressing C will run a check on the screen file to find any errors or possible
Xmistakes. Error messages starting '****' are fatal, and should certainly be
Xfixed. Errors starting '++++' are only warnings about non-standard design.
XAfter each message press any key to see the next. This test facility can be
Xused directly via the -t option.
X.PP
XWhen editing is finished, you can exit with 'q' to save the screen, or 'x' to
Xleave without a save. This will prompt for confirmation.
X.SH AUTHOR
XSteven Shipway. maujp@uk.ac.warwick.cu
X.PP
XLater additions: editor added by play@nl.cwi, help command by jason@uucp.aeras
X.SH FLAGS
X-s flag lists high-score chart.
X.PP
X-e flag enters editor.
X.PP
X-m flag enters hiscore table editor.
X.PP
X-c flag reads credits.
X.PP
X-f flag starts game with full screen play.
X.PP
X-v flag prints version.
X.PP
X-t flag tests screen.
X.PP
X-r flag records keypresses into given file.
X.SH SEE ALSO
Xdungeon, slay, adv, omega, hack, larn, moria, phantasia, /usr/games/*,
X/use/local/games/*
